    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2d36471b-5787-521f-824c-19b0424cab8b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/86/86c9b7da8fbc76a10fde6f35b50138b5cd53aae18e204be5e6e6f58562367183.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nI. $x\\in (-2,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in [0,2]$\n\nIII. $x\\in [-1,2]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- On interval I, $x\\in (-2,0]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval II, $x\\in [0,2]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval III, $x\\in [-1,2]$, the function is **not** invertible. Some horizontal lines will intersect the restricted graph more than once.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
